rance"}},"id":"bb97cd54edff4bb4abe8c8cee4aeec03","userType":"CONTRACTOR_GRANTEE","userId":"3d36226755384bcb8f395cff160d3824"},{"organizationId":"d7ca75575d34470aa8b3115ddef6df68","sequence":3,"submissionId":20260003024,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Madeleine Oliver"},"organization":{"name":"Amentum (United States)","location":"Chantilly, France"}},"id":"176322962d054c4086de64197c432f9d","userType":"OTHER","userId":"90f668d381294f4bafd37b69a3d3d6c8"},{"organizationId":"d7ca75575d34470aa8b3115ddef6df68","sequence":4,"submissionId":20260003024,"meta":{"author":{"orcidId":"","name":"Bruce Conger"},"organization":{"name":"Amentum (United States)","location":"Chantilly, France"}},"id":"30d7172b724b4b1897bcf33d6b725b9c","userType":"CONTRACTOR_GRANTEE","userId":"1873814205a44cc1ae73cdef6d96a3a6"}],"stiTypeDetails":"Conference Paper","technicalReviewType":"EXTERNAL_PEER_COMMITTEE","modified":"2026-04-22T11:43:52.7045070+00:00","id":20260003024,"created":"2026-04-13T19:35:29.6390870+00:00","center":{"code":"JSC","name":"Johnson Space Center","id":"dd46994b91a94cb2a2722617cbbadc55"},"onlyAbstract":false,"sensitiveInformation":2,"abstract":"To get from Moon to Mars, development of a Mars-centered spacesuit to support extravehicular activity (EVA) must begin now. In an effort toward this goal, setup of a Mars Portable Life Support System (PLSS) team to evaluate schematics for a Mars Extravehicular Exploration Mobility Unit (MxEMU) is underway. As part of a previous study, a wide range of potential architectures were evaluated and compared to determine leading options for a Martian PLSS. Going forward, these schematics will inform technology development, testing, detailed sizing analysis, and feasibility studies. A Mars PLSS Test Bed will be developed and used to assess the schematics on a breadboard style configuration of components. Following results of the test bed, a packaged Design Verification and Testing (DVT) unit will be designed to fully test the Mars PLSS with a Pressure Garment System (PGS), forming a prototype MxEMU. This paper will discuss the roadmap to Mars PLSS maturation and its integration into a prototype DVT unit. Technical considerations for Mars and high-level requirements will be compared to the Lunar exploration EMU (xEMU), and forward work to answer technology and knowledge gaps will be addressed.  ","isLessonsLearned":false,"disseminated":"DOCUMENT_AND_METADATA","cui":{"isCui":false,"submissionId":20260003024,"id":"f7c356667718483d932327286ed35719"},"meetings":[{"country":"PR","submissionId":20260003024,"endDate":"2026-07-16T04:00:00.0000000+00:00","sponsors":[{"organizationId":"66b67eba2c4d5e26a027207aa676a051","meta":{"organization":{"name":"Collins Aerospace (United States)","location":"Charlotte, United States"}},"meetingId":"7204643ecf2a4b1e957fa4e0427939df","id":"35bc2f7432b246ec95a72518d6ff8cd2"}],"name":"55th International Conference on Environmental Systems (ICES)","location":"Rio Grande","id":"7204643ecf2a4b1e957fa4e0427939df","startDate":"2026-07-12T05:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"publications":[{"submissionId":20260003024,"publisher":"International Conference on Environmental Systems","id":"04e22eb1b2104a5ab5bf1eba6d4b85b4","publicationDate":"2026-07-12T04:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"status":"CURATED","related":[{"disseminated":"DOCUMENT_AND_METADATA","id":20260005404,"type":"SEE_ALSO","title":"Mars Portable Life Support System Status and Plan","stiType":"PRESENTATION","distribution":"PUBLIC","status":"CURATED"}],"downloads":[{"draft":false,"mimetype":"application/pdf","name":"Final_ICES2026_Mars_PLSS_Plan.pdf","notes":"false positive","type":"STI","links":{"original":"/api/citations/20260003024/downloads/Final_ICES2026_Mars_PLSS_Plan.pdf","pdf":"/api/citations/20260003024/downloads/Final_ICES2026_Mars_PLSS_Plan.pdf","fulltext":"/api/citations/20260003024/downloads/Final_ICES2026_Mars_PLSS_Plan.pdf.txt"}}],"downloadsAvailable":true,"index":"submissions-2026-11-05-06-21"}